          "diff": "[ADD] * request method and returns the result JSON tree. It automatically fills the * cookie map with cookies in the result header after the request. * It logs the request warnings and adds makes sure that \"format\" : \"json\" * parameter is set. * * @param requestMethod * either POST or GET * @param parameters * Maps parameter keys to values. Out of this map the function * will create a query string for the request. * @return API result * @throws IOException * @throws MediaWikiApiErrorException if the API returns an error * / public JsonNode sendJsonRequest ( String requestMethod , Map < String , String > parameters ) throws IOException , MediaWikiApiErrorException { parameters.put ( ApiConnection.PARAM_FORMAT , \"json\" ) ; try ( InputStream response = sendRequest ( requestMethod , parameters ) ) { JsonNode root = this.mapper.readTree ( response ) ; this.checkErrors ( root ) ; this.logWarnings ( root ) ; return root ; } } / ** * Sends a request to the API with the given parameters and the given",
