          "content": "\t * anywhere, even over previously downloaded dump files that contain all"
        },
        {
          "b_line": 146,
          "a_line": 146,
          "content": "\t * versions. However, dump files may still contain non-current revisions,"
        },
        {
          "b_line": 147,
          "a_line": 147,
          "content": "\t * and when processing multiple dumps there might even be overlaps (one"
        },
        {
          "b_line": 148,
          "a_line": 148,
          "content": "\t * revision occurring in multiple dumps)."
        },
        {
          "b_line": 149,
          "a_line": 149,
          "content": "\t * <p>"
        },
        {
          "b_line": 150,
          "a_line": 150,
          "content": "\t * The result is ordered with the most recent dump first. If a dump file A"
        },
        {
          "b_line": 151,
          "a_line": 151,
          "content": "\t * contains revisions of a page P, and Rmax is the maximal revision of P in"
        },
        {
          "b_line": 152,
          "a_line": 152,
          "content": "\t * A, then every dump file that comes after A should contain only revisions"
        },
        {
          "b_line": 153,
          "a_line": 153,
          "content": "\t * of P that are smaller than or equal to Rmax. In other words, the maximal"
        },
        {
          "b_line": 154,
          "a_line": 154,
          "content": "\t * revision found in the first file that contains P at all should also be"
        },
        {
          "b_line": 155,
          "a_line": 155,
          "content": "\t * the maximal revision overall."
        },
        {
          "b_line": 156,
          "a_line": 156,
          "content": "\t * "
        },
        {
          "b_line": 157,
          "a_line": 157,
          "content": "\t * @param preferCurrent"
        },
        {
          "b_line": 158,
          "a_line": 158,
          "content": "\t *            should dumps with current revisions be preferred?"
        },
        {
          "b_line": 159,
          "a_line": 159,
          "content": "\t * @return an ordered list of all dump files that match the given criteria"
        },
        {
          "b_line": 160,
          "a_line": 160,
          "content": "\t */"
        },
